.\" OpenBSD-style concise man page
.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt TREE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tree
.Nd list contents of a directory in a tree-like format
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl adhV
.Op Fl L Ar n
.Op Fl I Ar pattern
.Op Fl Fl all
.Op Fl Fl directories-only
.Op Fl Fl level Ns = Ns Ar n
.Op Fl Fl ignore Ns = Ns Ar pattern
.Op Fl Fl color Ns = Ns Ar when
.Op Fl Fl icons Ns = Ns Ar when
.Op Fl Fl help
.Op Fl Fl version
.Op Ar directory ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility lists the contents of each
.Ar directory
operand as a tree, using UTF-8 box-drawing connectors.
Hidden names are omitted unless
.Fl a
is given.
If no operand is supplied, the current directory is listed.
.Pp
A directory symbolic link is printed as a leaf and is not
followed.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , Fl Fl all
Include entries whose names begin with a period.
.It Fl d , Fl Fl directories-only
List directories only.
The summary line then names directories and omits the file
count.
.It Fl L Ar n , Fl Fl level Ns = Ns Ar n
Descend at most
.Ar n
levels below each operand.
.Ar n
of 0 prints only the operand (a house deviation from Baker
.Nm tree ,
which rejects
.Fl L 0 ) .
.It Fl I Ar pattern , Fl Fl ignore Ns = Ns Ar pattern
Exclude names matching
.Ar pattern .
The flag is repeatable and cumulative.
A vertical bar inside
.Ar pattern
separates alternatives.
.It Fl Fl color Ns = Ns Ar when
Colorize names.
.Ar when
is
.Cm always ,
.Cm auto
(the default), or
.Cm never .
.Ev NO_COLOR
disables color even with
.Cm always .
.It Fl Fl icons Ns = Ns Ar when
Prefix entries with file-type icons.
.Ar when
uses the same values as
.Fl Fl color .
.Ev NO_COLOR
does not disable icons.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Display help and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl Fl version
Output version information and exit.
.El
.Pp
After all operands,
.Nm
prints a combined summary of the entries it listed.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std tree
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ tree src
$ tree -L 1 -d .
$ tree -I '*.log|skipme' project
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr find 1 ,
.Xr ls 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is not specified by POSIX.
Named flags follow Steve Baker's
.Nm tree
where this implementation includes them.
.Fl Fl color
and
.Fl h
as help follow vibeutils convention rather than Baker.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An vibeutils implementation by Travis Cole
